WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.936
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-Well, I always said
you make a great case.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.571
-You know, I saw you
debating DeSantis.
-Yeah.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.439
And I said, you know,
I'm trying to get this guy

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.941
to run for president
for a long time. (LAUGHS)

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.943
He looks like
he'd be very good at it.

00:00:11.076 --> 00:00:13.746
What I like with that also,
is that you're kind of mean,

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:14.747
-and we need that.
-(LAUGHS)

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.817
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-And, you know, when you need
to be not over the top.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.486
-But I was on--
-GAVIN NEWSOM:
No, I appreciate that.

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:22.188
-I was on KBLA.
-GAVIN: Yeah.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.323
The other day-- yesterday,
with my friend Tavis Smiley.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.726
-I'm an investor and a supporter
of that station.
-GAVIN: Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:29.062
And I-- You know, he said,
"Who do you want to run
for the president?"

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.863
I mentioned I think
you'd be good at the job,

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:32.131
not this year we know.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.933
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-(CHUCKLES)

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:36.268
No, I know. Um... (CHUCKLES)

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:38.371
But he said,
"I don't think he could win.

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.874
I don't think he could win.
He's too progressive.

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.108
-GAVIN: Yeah.
-Coming from this state,

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:46.712
and what he's done in this state
to win in any Southern state,
any red state."

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.081
I disagreed, but--

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:52.218
Now, this is a progressive,
African-American owned station,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.152
-and...
-GAVIN: Yeah.

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:54.153
...I'm sure they like you,

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.321
but he doesn't think
you can win.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.190
What do you say to that?
When you-- When your--

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.192
If you could win the--
Look at the... the...
the, uh, Swing states.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.694
-There's only eight of them.
-GAVIN: Right.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.397
Well, I mean, California
is an interesting case study,
isn't it?

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.032
It's the size
of 21-state populations
combined.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:08.033
BILL MAHER: Yeah.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.036
Two-thirds of the state
is very deeply red.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.006 line:0%
We don't need to be lectured
on rural, politics
or border issues.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.075 line:0%
I mean, in so many ways,
these are familiar issues.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.976 line:0%
And those issues
of the heartland
of the United States

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.846 line:0%
are very much a part and parcel
of the work we're doing
in this state.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.549 line:0%
But look,
I understand this notion
that you're from the coast,

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:24.817 line:0%
you don't understand
those things.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.786 line:0%
You can't talk the language,
you're not able to communicate.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.555
-BILL: Well--
-Uh, you're not able to
actually encourage

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:33.058
-and find that common ground.
-No, it's stuff like
there's a new law in this st--

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:35.628
I think we have
way too many regulations
and laws,

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.030
as we've talked about,
and this one, I think, says,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:43.203
"If you're a department store
with over 500 employees,

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.104
-you have to have
a gender-neutral...
-GAVIN: Oh, the toys.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.505
-...toy department.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.307
-BILL: Stuff like that...
-Yeah, I get it.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.310
-So, do you think that's silly?
-GAVIN: No,
but it's interesting.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.745
-BILL: You think that's
a silly thing that we have...
-What was interesting--

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:54.848
BILL: ...too much government...
too much government there.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.883
That-- Look,
that's an interesting one,

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.786
because the department stores
came to us supporting that.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.854
And they were once
making a case for that.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.423
They were making us--
They're already moving
in that direction.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.259
BILL: They wanted you
to make a law about them?

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.127
Well, they--
But they've supported
the legislation.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.862
Wasn't legislation
that was enacted,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.198
that was initiated
from my office,

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:13.399
but it was legislation
that came up

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.702
with interesting support
from the industry itself.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:18.003
But I understand
how that's exploited,

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.438
and good people can disagree.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:21.006
But that's not something
we woke up and said,

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.042
"This is a top priority
for the state,"

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:24.510
when we know that
the top priorities are

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.211
homelessness, housing,
the issues of crime,

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:27.213
quality of life,

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:29.082
and issues
related to regulation and taxes,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.483
which are all top of mind.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.085
-But I get how those things
are weaponized.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:36.588
All right.
So... While I got you here...

00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:37.857
-(GAVIN CHUCKLES)
-...'cause I live here,

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:39.191
-and I'm not going anywhere.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.860
So, I just want to make this
a better state

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.061
-like everybody else.
-GAVIN: Amen.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:44.496
And good job,
this year, making it rain.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.432
-GAVIN: You're welcome.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.167
-That was uh...
-That was so...

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.569
-Yeah.
-Because--

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.237
That was
my legislative priority.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.739
-Yes. Yeah.
-(LAUGHS) It was-- It was
looking bad there for a while,

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:55.341
and we still
don't have enough water

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.377
-in the Colorado River
and all this stuff.
-GAVIN: Yeah.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.844
And then, whenever I read,

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:01.814
80 percent of the water
goes to agriculture.

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:02.815
-Almonds.
-GAVIN: Right.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.316
No one ever asked you
about almonds?

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.684
Oh, I'm gonna ask you
about almonds.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.420
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:10.923
-We grow a boatload of almonds.
-GAVIN: I'm well aware.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.025
You know what,
you know how much-- How many--

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.927
-How much water it takes to--
-GAVIN: Many gallons.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.197
-Nineteen hundred gallons
to grow a pound of almonds.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.766
We-- Come on, man.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.000
-(GAVIN LAUGHING)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:23.502
-BILL: Take on big almonds.
-(LAUGHS) Take on big almonds.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.737
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.640
I mean, it's not like
we don't have the water.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.342
-GAVIN: No. But...
-But--

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.310
(HESITATES)
You're right about this.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.945
It's not that we don't have
the water that said.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.647
You know, the last couple years
were tough.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.949
I mean, it's-- But it's also
where the water is falling,

00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:37.950
and we're not capturing it.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.619
And we're not capturing
those extreme years

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.155 line:0%
with these atmospheric rivers.
Wets are getting a lot wetter,

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.956 line:0%
dry is drier,
hots are getting a lot hotter.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.958 line:0%
And so, we've got to modernize
our conveyance system,

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:47.493 line:0%
we've got to modernize
our storage,

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:49.294 line:0%
not just above ground
but below ground.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:51.497 line:0%
And so, that's a big part
of our focus and frame,

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.399
including desalinization plants.

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:55.801
We have 20 projects
just on desal

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.469
that we're working on today,
so we've been--

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.739
We put out
a detailed water strategy

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:00.873
that includes-- By the way,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.210
getting that
Delta conveyance project
back up and operational,

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:08.747
and includes the first
above ground off-stream
storage facility

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.484
in half a century in the state,
which, by the way,

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:14.687
is being aided
by a regulatory package
I pushed forward

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.923
to reduce red tape
in the state of California,

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.926
address the permitting quagmires
that you rightfully pointed out.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.994
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:26.466
-See you're... (LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:29.902
You're good at this.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.070
-What... (LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:32.671
BILL: See, I'm telling you,
you're good at this job.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.875
-Okay, but-- (LAUGHS)
No, sit down. Okay, but--
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.276
But here's anot--

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.245
I feel like
the last couple of years,

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.914
you've, like,
purposefully picked this fight
with the red states.

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:43.015
-I mean, the DeSantis--
-Yeah.

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:45.318
Yeah, but I don't wanna live
in the Civil War country.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:46.618
-GAVIN: I agree with that.
-You know what?

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:47.686
-GAVIN: I--
-But you seem like,

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:51.557
you purposely wanna set up
this... this dichotomy between--

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.060
Oh, this is a blue state,
and that's a red state,

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.062
-and I don't wanna live
in that country.
-I love that.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.063
BILL: I like Florida.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.599
-I'm with you, and by the way,
I like Florida as well.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.701
Like-- I like all these states.
I completely agree.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.002
I don't wanna
have a state of mind

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.937
that's in constant
fight-or-flight.
We've gone through so much.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.939
We've been
polarized and traumatized.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:09.275
This has been
a tough five, six years
across the globe,

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:10.776
not just in this country.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.412
That said, I'm not gonna
sit back and watch,

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:15.915
and you made the point
just a moment ago
in your monologue.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:16.916
You got folks out there,

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:19.218
trying to bring us back
to a pre-1960s world.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:20.519
America in reverse.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:23.322
Rolling back voting rights,
LGBTQ rights, women's rights,

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.958
not just access to abortion,
but contraception.

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:28.227
I mean, it's a profound
and consequential moment.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.595
And you could sit by and say,

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:30.996
"Well,
I really wanna get along,"

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.199
as these guys
are rolling back the clock.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:35.100
Or you can stand tall
and assert yourself.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.403
And the reason I started to go
into those red states,

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:39.371
the reason
I started to take on DeSantis,

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.774
and the reason
I started doing ads
in these red states

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:44.043
is I didn't feel
my party was doing enough.

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:47.947
It was CRT, one year,
then it's ESG, and it's DEI,

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.216
anything with three letters,
these guys keep coming.

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:52.284
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-And they're shape-shifting.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.787
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-And they're-- I mean,
they're char-- And, so...

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:55.821
But it's true, right.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:06:00.092
And so... And I just thought
there was a little timidity
in our party.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:01.961
And I thought
we need to call this stuff out.

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:04.663
These guys are being
on a banning binge
across this country.

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.064
You want to talk
about cancel culture,

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:07.600
look at the Republican Party.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.536
Ask Bud Light, target Disney.
That's just the private sector.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:12.905
Banning speech
is not just in the classroom,

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:15.574
but in the boardroom
as it relates to issues of race.

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:19.544
Look what they've done,
3,362 books just last year.

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:20.580
They're banning.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.214
This is a serious
and consequential moment.

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.550
It's the cultural purge
that's going on in this country

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:27.619
And so, I just felt like
we needed to call that out
as democrats,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.288
and put them on the defensive,

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:33.058
since we're consistently
on our heels
as a Democratic party.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:36.162
Even though I think
the facts bear out our case

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:40.533
-significantly better
than the case on the other side.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:06:43.135 --> 00:06:47.673
But again, Bill, I say all that
with love in my heart...

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:49.508
-(LAUGHS)
-...with love in my heart,

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:52.077
and I mean that, I mean,
I don't talk down to people...

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.213
-BILL: Can you-- (CLEARS THROAT)
-...I don't wanna talk
past people.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.716
Everyone wants to be respected,
connected and protected,

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:58.784
and we all want to be loved
and need to be loved.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.187
I'm with you on all that.
At the same time, man,

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.255
when you're going after
the LGBT community

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:05.290
and talking down to people
and humiliating folks,

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:08.060
you're threatening to sue
the special Olympians,

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:10.162
when you're going after
the Black community

00:07:10.295 --> 00:07:12.698
and trying to rewrite history
and saying slavery somehow

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.500
was some workforce
development program,

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:18.871
-damn it, we have to call
that stuff out.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:20.906
(CHUCKLES) Okay.

00:07:21.039 --> 00:07:22.642
-GAVIN: Off of my high horse.
-Oh, you were.

00:07:25.243 --> 00:07:27.480
-Can you teach that speech
to Biden?
-(GAVIN CHUCKLES)

